<lines>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_1">pretium legale, &amp; vulgare iustum illae</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_2">circustantiae, &amp; rationes sunt aestiman¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_3">dae, &amp; examinandae, quia ratio eas natu¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_4">ralis dictat: ergo similiter in pretio con¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_5">uentionali, licet illud habeat maiorem</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_6">latitudinem. Quartò, quia rationes in</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_7">contrarium parum, aut nihil vrgent.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_8">Ad primum respondetur, leges</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_9">illas esse necessariò interpretandas, vt</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_10">antinomia tollatur cum alijs legibus ci¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_11">tatis; &amp; leges illas, quae pro illa opinio¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_12">ne citantur, solum velle pretium con¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_13">uentionale non esse taxatum lege, aut</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_14">consuetudine; &amp; ideo recurrendum ne¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_15">cessario esse ad voluntatem contrahen¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_16">tium; sed non quidem irrationabilem,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_17">&amp; effrenatam, sed eisdem rationibus</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_18">perpensis, quę ideo magis expatiatur in</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_19">pretio, &amp; maiorem habet latitudinem,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_20">sed non immensam, &amp; exorbitantem,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_21">&amp; quemlibet esse suae rei moderatorem,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_22">&amp; arbitrum, vt vendat eam, sed iusto pretio.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_23">Ad secundum enim, respondetur esse</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_24">ex quo pretium illud determinetur, li¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_25">cet maiori quadam latitudine, nempe</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_26">ex iudicio prudentum perpensis cir¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_27">cumstantij, de quibus infra subijcimus.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_28">Ad tertium respondetur; etiam</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_29">res ad voluntatem, &amp; voluptatem com¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_30">paratas iusto pretio distrahi debere;</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_31">quia multoties res illae quantumuis su¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_32">perfluae videantur sunt necessariae ad</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_33">statum: quis enim dubitet nobiles cogi</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_34">ad emendas pretiosas vestes, &amp; Duces,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_35">&amp; Marchiones, &amp; Reges ad emendas</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_36">cemmas, &amp; alendos canes, &amp; falcones.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_37">Tum vel maximè, quia etiam si omninò</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_38">superfluae essent, vt ait D. Augustinus</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_39">supra, omnes volunt vili emere, &amp; caro</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_40">vendere, &amp; semper cogentur saltem suo</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_41">affectu ad emendum, vnde non gratis</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_42">donant, sed coacti caro emunt, vt infra</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_43">magis liquebit.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_44">Sit ergo prima regula posita, &amp; con¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_45">stitutissima in his, quae damus pro ijs,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_46">quae non sunt attendenda ad iustum</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_47">pretium in emptionibus constituendum</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_48">esse vitiosam, &amp; reprobatam regulam</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_49">rem tantum valere, quanti vendi po¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_50">test etiam in pretio conuentionali.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_51">Secunda regula sit, non esse atten¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_52">dendam perfectionem rei venditae in</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_53">esse naturae, sic enim pretiosior esset</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_54">mus, vel musca domo, quantumuis ma¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_55">gna vel auro, &amp; gemma. Nam sicut D.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_56">Aug. ait lib. Io. de ciuit. cap. 16. L. Quis non</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_57">magis velit domi habere panes, quam</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_58">mures, &amp; nummos, quam pullices? Jita¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_59">que licet illa in esse naturae sint perfe¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_60">ctiora in commutationibus, &amp; commer¬</line>
</lines>
